  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nhello, we deleted some rows from the events table, i know it s bad\r\nbut there was too much of a sensitive data we needed to rip off.\r\nNow, on that room we get 'Room X does not exist' as soon as we try to push any event (post new messages)\r\nWhat is the way to recover the state of that room without creating a new one\r\n\r\nIn the database and on RIOT, the room still exists with valid memberships.\r\nAnd the creation event (and all of but 2 events of that room) are still there.\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\nhomeserver: custom\r\nVersion de riot-web : 0.13.4\r\nmatrix: 0.26.0\r\n\r\n- **Install method**: docker (https://github.com/corpusops/docker-matrix)\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/master/synapse/event_auth.py#L70\r\n\r\n- here the value auth_events is ``{}``, if we change the test is on a boolean value (``if not auth_events``), rather than None, we can post messages, but it seems hacky and not a solution. \r\n- Indeed, as soon as we remember this \"bypass test\", we can't post anymore to that failed room.\r\n- Of course, The multiple posts are done with a loggued in user, which is a member of that room\r\n\r\n",
